# Normal desktop apps — spec section 20. Kept intentionally modest so the
# security/pentest categories remain the visual and functional center of
# the OS, not the desktop layer.

firefox-esr
okular
libreoffice
kde-spectacle
kdenlive
gwenview
ark
kcalc
vlc
bluedevil

# `spectacle` was the wrong Debian package name — the actual package is
# `kde-spectacle` (confirmed against packages.debian.org). `klipper` has
# no installable bookworm package at all (only exists as a library in
# trixie/sid, not a standalone app in bookworm) — removed rather than
# left broken. Nothing lost functionally: KDE Plasma's clipboard history
# is provided by plasma-workspace's own built-in clipboard plasmoid, not
# a separate klipper package, in this Debian version.
